youtube-dl is a '''command-line program''' to download videos from ''YouTube.com'' and other video sites. It is a popular, open-source tool that allows users to easily download videos from various online platforms. The program is written in ''Python'' and is available for ''UNIX''-based systems, including ''Linux'' and ''macOS'', as well as ''Windows''.

== Overview ==
youtube-dl is a '''free software''' project that provides a simple and efficient way to download videos from online platforms. The program supports a wide range of video sites, including ''YouTube'', ''Vimeo'', and ''Dailymotion''. It is highly customizable, allowing users to specify various options, such as video quality, format, and output file name.

=== Features ===
Some of the key features of youtube-dl include:
* '''Video downloading''': youtube-dl allows users to download videos from various online platforms.
* '''Format selection''': users can choose from a variety of video formats, including ''MP4'', ''WebM'', and ''FLV''.
* '''Video quality selection''': users can select the video quality, ranging from ''1080p'' to ''240p''.
* '''Output template''': users can specify a custom output template for the downloaded video files.
* '''Configuration''': youtube-dl can be configured to suit individual user needs, including options for proxy settings, user agent, and more.

== Installation ==
To install youtube-dl, users can follow these steps:
* For ''UNIX''-based systems, including ''Linux'' and ''macOS'', users can install youtube-dl using '''curl''' or '''wget'''. The installation command is: <code>sudo curl -L https://yt-dl.org/downloads/latest/youtube-dl -o /usr/local/bin/youtube-dl</code> or <code>sudo wget https://yt-dl.org/downloads/latest/youtube-dl -O /usr/local/bin/youtube-dl</code>.
* For ''Windows'' users, an '''exe file''' can be downloaded from the [official website](https://yt-dl.org/latest/youtube-dl.exe) and placed in any location on the system ''PATH''.
* Alternatively, users can install youtube-dl using '''pip''': <code>sudo -H pip install --upgrade youtube-dl</code>.
* ''macOS'' users can also install youtube-dl using '''Homebrew''' or '''MacPorts''': <code>brew install youtube-dl</code> or <code>sudo port install youtube-dl</code>.

== Configuration ==
youtube-dl can be configured to suit individual user needs. Users can specify options such as proxy settings, user agent, and more. The configuration file can be found in the ''~/.config/youtube-dl'' directory.

== Output Template ==
The output template can be customized to specify the output file name and format. Users can use various placeholders, such as ''%(title)s'' and ''%(id)s'', to create a custom output template.

== Format Selection ==
youtube-dl allows users to select from a variety of video formats, including ''MP4'', ''WebM'', and ''FLV''. Users can specify the format using the '''-f''' option, followed by the format code.

== Video Selection ==
Users can select the video quality, ranging from ''1080p'' to ''240p''. The video quality can be specified using the '''-f''' option, followed by the quality code.

